{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Bel bows down.</b> An idol of the Babylonians; likewise Nebo, and some say it is the star of the sun." "<b>Qores.</b> From the root of קרסים (clasps) (Exodus 26:11), and the meaning is known, and it is not fitting to write it." "<b>To the living beast and to the animal.</b> That a man would carry them upon them." "<b>Therefore. Your carriers are loaded, a burden to the weary.</b> A description of the beast that carries."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:16.798974724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}